6 25 on your friday morning what's cool  at school how about some wicked smart ko  knutson middle school students they're  in the top 10 for a chance at a hundred  thousand dollars from samsung to make  what might sound like a crazy idea into  reality  sixth and seventh graders in steve  gaskill's science class found a problem  bus stops get so hot that people won't  often sit on the benches because they  are afraid that they will get burned the  solution they came up with wasn't just  right around the corner it's in the  school's backyard the bus stop buyer  school has steel benches which feel very  hot in the summer  so we researched alternative materials  we could use to replace the steel  one material that stood out to us was  lightweight concrete made from sunflower  stalks  we already grow sunflowers in our school  garden and normally the old stocks just  go in the trash  after learning about sunflower stock  concrete we decided to recycle last  year's stocks  we shredded the stocks and used them to  replace gravel in a standard concrete  mix but the kids didn't stop there  taking their story to the regional  transportation commission  man sunflower stock concrete all right  shout out to 8th grader ivey fewer born  for making that video and to the well  spoken sixth grader callie pippin so  getting to the final ten with the other  schools from around the country has  already won the local kids 50 grand but  you can help them win it all by voting  for them we got the link in the online  version of this story at 8newsnow.com if  you know something that's cool at school  let us know cool it's cool under the  community tab at 8newsnow.com or just  email cool at school at eightnewsnow.com
 

